  "implementation_findings": [
    "One normal tracker call followed by one audit call uses the actual same IntentStore; no retries, added model, training, or target-specific branch.",
    "Audit receives all existing IDs including withdrawn records and arrived raw dialogue; labels, focal IDs, expected states, case metadata and old error-bearing histories are excluded.",
    "Strict JSON/schema, exact once-per-ID coverage, arrived user evidence, value/verdict consistency, owner/status-only operations, atomic commits and stale-snapshot rejection are enforced.",
    "Insufficient evidence holds the whole record; unsupported owner-plus-withdrawal transitions are explicitly unresolved. No new intent, text rewrite, deletion, or task execution is allowed.",
    "Fixed base revision/files, adapter config/weights and active enabled adapter identity are verified. Evaluation mode and zero trainable parameters are checked at every call.",
    "Manifest hashes/sizes, source freeze, independent receipt, 24-call ceiling, final durable count/order, per-call raw output and error journals make collection auditable.",
    "Core 14-test and pipeline 4-test first-pass logs were inspected, not rerun. Their scripted reports establish structural behavior only."
  ],
  "resolved_findings": [
    "Collector now verifies every frozen manifest file and bound source before model load, and rejects Python optimized mode.",
    "Pipeline package import now uses the relative import path with script fallback.",
    "Concurrent new arrivals now return stale_input/not_run_stale_input, retain current state and do not issue an extra audit call.",
    "Collector now requires durable call count, ordinal sequence and case/stage sequence before reporting collection completed."
  ],
